            <ArticleTitle>The use of magnetic resonance imaging in diagnosing Wilms' tumor mimicking a lumbosacral strain and sprain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>455-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Wilms' tumor is the most common tumor of the kidney in childhood. This article discusses the case of a young adult with a Wilms' tumor whose initial presentation appeared similar to a lumbosacral strain. The use of magnetic resonance imaging in diagnosing Wilms' tumor is discussed, along with the common clinical picture of the disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
